Naming is the act of giving a name to an individual, typically a monster, which profoundly affects their growth and capabilities. 

There are three main methods of naming: Equal Naming, where the namer and named establish an equal relationship with minimal energy expenditure; 

Master-Subordinate Naming, where the named becomes subordinate to the namer, requiring proportional energy expenditure and carrying risks such as energy loss; 

Named by the Masses, where an individual receives a name through collective belief, granting power and self-image enhancements without forming a close bond. 

Named monsters experience a significant increase in strength, intelligence, and abilities compared to their previous state. This enhancement is a result of the soul bond formed between the namer and the named, empowering the latter with heightened capabilities. Named Individuals frequently evolve into their next evolution, substantially increasing in power and competence.

